{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/112373-large-changeling-population-and-end-game-bosses","id":112373,"title":"large changeling population and end-game bosses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-13T19:15:05-07:00","id":112373,"title":"large changeling population and end-game bosses","content":"First off, this is my first time on this forum so bear with me. I'm thinking of writing a chronicle for changeling with a large population in mind. The number would be around 120 something because the number of surrounding trods. My reasoning is that I wanted to add a lot of things from the changeling books and my own ideas for my players to mess with. Another thing I like about having a large population is the chance for very Fae-like politics with every weird looking slob having three or more titles. Now, how my freehold would work is that most of the power-players run a very successful Casino/hotel with some nice connections with local crime.<br /> <br /> My other question is if my players wanted, (I know one does) to have more action in the game, I was thinking of having a Promethean or Magath be a secret endboss of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2720-theoctopusman","name":"theoctopusman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T01:47:26-07:00","id":112487,"title":"","content":"Having a large population can work fine. Some places have a lot of surrounding trods and are easy to get to from Faerie. Having a game in a larger city can have a definite charm.<br /> <br /> Is a Magath a Mage? If so, they don't make for such good boss fights as subtle enemies. If you want a downright crazy throwdown, go for a Sin-Eater or Mummy...both can come back from the dead and both can do some downright spectacular effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T07:51:31-07:00","id":112635,"title":"","content":"A magath is a hybrid spirit without a choir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T09:40:24-07:00","id":112710,"title":"","content":"I'll advice using anything outside of the Changeling line as an endboss for your players. Mages could work but Promethans seems like they have so few points of contact with the Lost that it might not at all feel very personal.<br /> <br /> A suggestion for an end boss I would make is an Exiled Fae who hides within the Freehold who, if things goes roughly accoriding to plan, enters the Hedge to return to Arcadia and end its exile and the players gets to confront this True Fae on the road back. That way it might be more personal, especially if they in the end can connect manner of chaos and mayhem to this Fae, and prevent it from getting away with a ton of info about the Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T13:04:37-07:00","id":112891,"title":"","content":"Well a left-handed mage would sound pretty cool, I have the idea of having the promethean/magath/whatever have a large amount of rumors surrounding it in some abandoned corner of the city. My Magath idea would have a Egyptian crocodile spirit who ate the spirits of machines and smoke from an island processing plant of some kind. The Crocodile Magath would kinda be like the ticktock croc from peter pan. I really think that the spirits in Nwod is pretty cool and I have a small list of ones I made including a ancient prey spirit in the shape of a mammoth sized Guinea-pig.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2720-theoctopusman","name":"theoctopusman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}